**Figure B.2: IAGH TEE 3.2 Hardware Architecture.** The trusted execution environment is built around an isolated Security Co‑Processor (right) that enforces policy limits on the main AI Accelerator (left) through physical mechanisms: an analogue current‑shunt FLOP limiter, a token‑bucket memory bandwidth controller, and a whitelist‑based network interface. The security co‑processor hosts a PUF‑based root of trust, a cryptographic accelerator for licence validation and session key derivation, a real‑time anomaly detector, and a tamper‑detection mesh. A physical MOSFET kill‑switch with four activation paths provides irreversible termination. Secure logging uses write‑once anti‑fuse memory. Full specifications appear in Chapter 6, with formal verification in Section 6.5 and cryptographic protocols in Chapter 7.

