# Appendix C – CBOR License Encoding Specification

## C.1 Introduction

This appendix defines the Concise Binary Object Representation (CBOR) encoding for ZENITH terrestrial agent licences as specified in Section 6.2. CBOR (RFC 8949) is chosen for its compactness, explicit typing, and suitability for constrained environments such as the IAGH TEE 3.2 security co‑processor. The encoding is self‑describing, deterministic, and designed to be verified byte‑for‑byte during licence validation.

## C.2 CBOR Data Model Mapping

The abstract licence structure from Section 6.2 is mapped to CBOR as follows:

| JSON Field                     | CBOR Major Type | CBOR Encoding Notes                                                                 |
|--------------------------------|-----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `version`                      | unsigned integer | Major type 0, encoded as uint 8 (value 3 for TEE 3.2)                               |
| `license_id`                   | text string     | Major type 3, UUID URN format, deterministic length                                 |
| `issuer`                       | text string     | Major type 3, NASAg region code, e.g., "NASAg-EU-003"                               |
| `device_id`                    | byte string     | Major type 2, 32‑byte PUF‑derived device identifier (binary)                        |
| `validity`                     | map             | Major type 5, containing `not_before` and `not_after` keys                          |
| `validity.not_before`          | tag 1 (epoch)   | Tag 1 (CBOR epoch date/time), RFC 3339 equivalent as integer (seconds since 1970)   |
| `validity.not_after`           | tag 1           | As above                                                                             |
| `compute_limits`               | map             | Major type 5                                                                         |
| `compute_limits.maximum_flops` | text string     | Scientific notation string, e.g., "1.0e+25"                                         |
| `compute_limits.sustained_percentage` | unsigned     | Major type 0, integer 0–100                                                         |
| `compute_limits.burst_allowance`       | map         | Nested map with `multiplier` (float), `window_ms` (uint), `cooling_period_ms` (uint) |
| `memory_limits`                | map             | Major type 5, `bandwidth_gbs` (uint), `capacity_gb` (uint)                          |
| `network_restrictions`         | map             | Allowed endpoints as array of CBOR byte strings (IP prefixes), ports as array of uint, protocols as array of text strings, bandwidth_mbps as uint |
| `purpose_restrictions`         | map             | `allowed_use_cases` and `prohibited_use_cases` as arrays of text URIs, `geographic_restrictions` as array of text strings (GeoJSON polygons) |
| `monitoring_requirements`      | map             | `telemetry_interval_s` (uint), `required_metrics` (array of text), `reporting_endpoints` (array of text URLs) |
| `violation_policy`             | map             | `levels` as array of maps, each with `threshold` (text), `action` (text)            |
| `signature`                    | map             | `algorithm` (text), `value` (byte string), `certificate_chain` (array of byte strings) |

All keys are encoded as CBOR text strings (major type 3) with deterministic ordering: keys are sorted by their CBOR encoding length, then lexicographically, to produce a canonical byte sequence for signing.

